===persian===

بعد از جنگ
با هر آتش می‌لرزم...
نابود باد همهٔ آتش‌ها
مگر،
خورشید، مهتاب، فانوس... و
شعلهٔ مهربانِ نگاهِ تو...
بیا به غار برگردیم،
دیوارها منتظرند... و
خاطرم پر از تصویرهای تازه است...
۱۳۶۹/۶/۷

===machine===

After the war
I tremble at every fire...
Let all fires be destroyed
except
the sun, the moonlight, the lantern... and
the kind flame of your gaze...
Come, let us go back to the cave,
the walls are waiting... and
my memory is full of fresh images...
1369/6/7

===lantern===

After the war
every fire makes me shake...
Let all fires be destroyed
except
the sun, the moonlight, the lantern — and
the kind flame of your looking...
Come, let us go back to the cave.
The walls are waiting... and
my head is full of new pictures...

1369/6/7

===translation===

===footnotes===

The cave whose walls are waiting is the studio: a painter reaching past his own century for
the oldest room where images were put on rock. It arrives one line after a wish that every fire on
earth be destroyed — and cave painting is made by firelight.
